00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:05.310
but how do people know
about these things?

00:35:05.310 --> 00:35:06.540
How do we tell our customers?

00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:08.320
Because that's
really what we want.

00:35:08.320 --> 00:35:12.240
So a couple of ways,
just to let people know.

00:35:12.240 --> 00:35:15.680
The way that you could trigger
this explicitly is by going,

00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:20.280
"OK, so-and-so, talk to
'the name of the action'."

00:35:20.280 --> 00:35:23.550
And so our canonical example
that we use is Personal Chef.

00:35:23.550 --> 00:35:26.040
And so we're just
telling Google,

00:35:26.040 --> 00:35:27.755
"I want to talk to this action."

00:35:27.755 --> 00:35:29.130
You could also do
something where

00:35:29.130 --> 00:35:30.880
you can bypass the
welcome and go straight

00:35:30.880 --> 00:35:33.430
into the interactivity
that you want.

00:35:33.430 --> 00:35:34.890
And so an example
is, "OK, Google--

00:35:34.890 --> 00:35:36.838
ah, dang it, I said it.

00:35:36.838 --> 00:35:37.337
So sorry.

00:35:37.337 --> 00:35:43.410
So sorry-- ask Personal
Chef for a hot soup recipe."

00:35:43.410 --> 00:35:45.060
So for the demo
that I filled out,

00:35:45.060 --> 00:35:49.680
it would be something like,
"OK, sure, sure, sure, ask

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:55.074
My Bike Demo if mountain
bike tires are in stock."

00:35:55.074 --> 00:35:57.240
That way, it bypasses the
welcome and all that jazz.

00:35:57.240 --> 00:35:58.959
So our users are
getting really great

00:35:58.959 --> 00:36:00.750
interactivity and
getting to what they want

00:36:00.750 --> 00:36:04.071
to get done earlier and faster.

00:36:04.071 --> 00:36:05.820
Another way to be able
to get your actions

00:36:05.820 --> 00:36:08.040
triggered is
implicit triggering.

00:36:08.040 --> 00:36:11.640
This has to do with
just asking Google,

00:36:11.640 --> 00:36:14.770
"I want to do a
thing like this."

00:36:14.770 --> 00:36:20.067
And this gets really similar to
when you just go to our website

00:36:20.067 --> 00:36:21.150
and you type something in.

00:36:21.150 --> 00:36:24.270
It gives you the best
results based off

00:36:24.270 --> 00:36:27.360
of some really great algorithms.

00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:29.220
And it will try to
surface the action

00:36:29.220 --> 00:36:32.320
that Google thinks is best
for the user at that time.

00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:36.940
So here are some examples
of implicit triggering.

00:36:36.940 --> 00:36:37.982
We also have a directory.

00:36:37.982 --> 00:36:39.523
So what I mentioned
earlier, you want

00:36:39.523 --> 00:36:41.200
to put in all your
information, so we

00:36:41.200 --> 00:36:44.530
do have a directory where I
know I love to go in there

00:36:44.530 --> 00:36:47.260
and just check out what
other people are doing,

00:36:47.260 --> 00:36:49.970
see what's going on.

00:36:49.970 --> 00:36:51.590
So there's that.

00:36:51.590 --> 00:36:55.120
And then this one I think
is the most impactful way

00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:56.890
to communicate, is action links.

00:36:56.890 --> 00:36:59.740
And so you could link
your Action from anywhere.

00:36:59.740 --> 00:37:02.116
So let's say you have a social
media campaign that you're

00:37:02.116 --> 00:37:04.490
building now and you want to
highlight that you spent all

00:37:04.490 --> 00:37:05.920
this time building this Action.

00:37:05.920 --> 00:37:08.020
You can actually
have a URL that could

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:10.660
post on Twitter or any
other social media platform

00:37:10.660 --> 00:37:14.800
and send your users straight
to the Action itself.

00:37:14.800 --> 00:37:18.350
So that's another
capability, too.

00:37:18.350 --> 00:37:20.800
So here's a list
of all resources.

00:37:20.800 --> 00:37:22.650
That way you have
everything you need.

00:37:22.650 --> 00:37:24.500
Yeah, photos, please.

00:37:24.500 --> 00:37:27.430
Like to put this at
the end, that way,

00:37:27.430 --> 00:37:29.450
I believe, almost
everything I mentioned.

00:37:29.450 --> 00:37:31.620
Here's a great
starting point for it.

00:37:37.980 --> 00:37:39.880
All our resources on there.

00:37:39.880 --> 00:37:43.000
Of course, we have our
own code labs and samples,

00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:44.290
things exist out there.

00:37:44.290 --> 00:37:49.540
Something I did really gloss
over completely was design.

00:37:49.540 --> 00:37:51.850
When it comes to
building your Action,

00:37:51.850 --> 00:37:55.360
we have a lot of great,
rich design documentation.

00:37:55.360 --> 00:37:58.450
I know when I was building my
first Action, as a developer,

00:37:58.450 --> 00:38:02.450
I saw design and I was like,
skip, skip, skip, skip.

00:38:02.450 --> 00:38:05.000
That bit me in the tushie later.

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:07.230
That was not a good idea.

00:38:07.230 --> 00:38:09.974
So please learn from me
and be better than me.

00:38:09.974 --> 00:38:11.390
Really check out
the documentation

00:38:11.390 --> 00:38:14.000
when it comes to design,
because there are many times

00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:17.810
where you're building this
out and you could get lost

00:38:17.810 --> 00:38:20.330
in the conversation, and where
you're at in the conversation

00:38:20.330 --> 00:38:23.390
flow, or what type of
phrases people might use.

00:38:23.390 --> 00:38:26.600
So I definitely highly
recommend go to the design docs,

00:38:26.600 --> 00:38:28.731
write out the physical
conversations people might

00:38:28.731 --> 00:38:30.980
be having, and using that
as your template versus just

00:38:30.980 --> 00:38:32.790
trying to live code it.

00:38:32.790 --> 00:38:34.810
We have great documentation
in regards to that.

00:38:34.810 --> 00:38:38.180
We even have a code lab designed
for designing your Action as

00:38:38.180 --> 00:38:38.940
well.

00:38:38.940 --> 00:38:40.495
So that's that.

00:38:40.495 --> 00:38:41.870
This is a way that
you could stay

00:38:41.870 --> 00:38:45.980
connected, if you're interested,
on Actions on Google, being

00:38:45.980 --> 00:38:49.260
part of the cool kids' club
and building your action.

00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:54.980
So we're active on Google+, and
of course, our developers page,

00:38:54.980 --> 00:38:56.224
and then on Twitter.

00:38:56.224 --> 00:38:57.640
If you build
anything out, I would

00:38:57.640 --> 00:38:58.980
love to know what you've done.

00:38:58.980 --> 00:39:00.620
You could use the
hashtag #AoGDevs.

00:39:00.620 --> 00:39:02.870
That's something that we are
usually checking out just

00:39:02.870 --> 00:39:04.940
to see what people are building.

00:39:04.940 --> 00:39:07.351
Then there's my contact
information down there.

00:39:07.351 --> 00:39:07.850
Thank you.

00:39:07.850 --> 00:39:09.260
I appreciate it.

00:39:09.260 --> 00:39:10.760
